# Cap Chain (Zero-Ambient)

main(bind, fs, sys, env, time, fs_w, args)
  -> run_ooda_mcp(bind, fw, fs, env, sys, args)
    -> mcp_server_run(bind, fw, fs, env, t)
      -> mcp_transport_read(bind, fw, fs, t)
      -> mcp_dynamic_load(fs, path)                          # G9 cold-start
      -> mcp_server_handle_body(fs, session, graph, codex, body)
        -> mcp_session_seen_id                                # R5 replay gate
        -> mcp_dispatch_orient
        -> mcp_dispatch_decide                                # phase + tier + URI allowlist
        -> mcp_dispatch_cap_audit                             # R7 runtime audit
        -> mcp_dispatch_act_resource_read (uses cache.graph_json)  # Item 1
        -> mcp_dispatch_act_resource_read_stream              # Item 2
        -> mcp_dispatch_etag_matches                          # G6 versioning
        -> mcp_sampling_root_allows                           # scope enforcement
        -> mcp_dynamic_record                                 # G7 dynamic graph log
      -> mcp_dynamic_fold + mcp_gossip_merge                 # G7 + G8
      -> mcp_dynamic_persist                                 # G9 cold-start write
      -> mcp_redteam_run_all                                  # Item 3 / G10

# REDTEAM R1-R8

R1 subversion: PASS — caps minted by runtime; no string-forged caps.
R2 exhaustion: PASS — 256-msg cap removed; loop terminates on shutdown/close/EOF.
R3 obfuscation: PASS — lsp_jsonrpc_escape on every string field.
R4 injection:   PASS — mcp_orient_uri_is_canonical gates URIs to 6 values.
R5 replay:      PASS — mcp_session_seen_id returns -32603 on duplicate id.
R6 traversal:   PASS — mcp_sampling_root_allows rejects non-ooda:// outside roots.
R7 escalation:  PASS (RUNTIME) — mcp_dispatch_cap_audit returns -32603 if caller lacks cap.
R8 integrity:   PASS — mcp_codex_gold_master_sha computes real SHA-256 of LLMS.oot.
                All 8 gates now also fire periodically via mcp_redteam_run_all.

# Six Items Closed (Phase 1)

Item 1 (E-M cache):       McpCodexCache keyed by (path, size_bytes); mcp_codex_resolve_cached returns 0/1/2.
Item 2 (G3+ tier):        McpSession.tier declared in initialize.params; -32604 envelope.
Item 3 (G6 versioning):   codexVersion = 8-char SHA prefix; If-None-Match returns -32606.
Item 4 (sampling/roots):  mcp_sampling.oo exposes refusal + root scope.
Item 5 (G7 dynamic):      mcp_graph_dynamic.oo with record/fold/persist/load.
Item 6 (R7 audit):        mcp_dispatch_cap_audit (bit-encoded) gates required caps.

# Three More Items Closed (Phase 2)

Item 7 (G9 cold-start):  mcp_dynamic_load is real (parses persisted JSON).
Item 8 (G8 gossip):      mcp_gossip_merge dedups by (kind, name).
Item 9 (OODA Act stream): mcp_stream_build emits notifications/progress frames.

# Three More Items Closed (Phase 3 — Latest Sprint)

Item A (E-M cache hit):   mcp_dispatch_act_resource_read takes graph_json; server passes cache.graph_json.
Item B (OODA Act boards): mcp_dispatch_act_resource_read_stream emits per-board frames + final result.
Item C (G10 redteam):     mcp_redteam.oo fires 8 probes; mcp_server_run calls mcp_redteam_run_all on close.

# G11 / G12 / G13 — Set Up (Next-Horizon)

G11 self-certification: mcp_horizon.oo:mcp_g11_self_certify(g) stub.
G12 federation:         mcp_horizon.oo:mcp_g12_federate(local, peer_count) stub.
G13 codex lineage:      mcp_horizon.oo:mcp_g13_lineage_append(sha, board_count) stub.

Each stub returns "" (or a stub marker) to signal "not yet wired." A future
sprint will implement real behavior: G11 enumerates the graph's claimed caps
and verifies each, G12 merges peer graphs over a real transport, G13 tracks
the LLMS.oot file mtime and appends versioned entries on change.

# Removed Obsolete Paths

Before                                            After
- mcp_take_json_object (hand-rolled)              -> shared LSP table parser
- 256-message hard cap in mcp_process_stream       -> unbounded loop
- mcp_codex_embedded (47-line text blob)           -> mcp_codex_gold_master_sha (real SHA)
- 5-path heuristic probe                           -> 2-path deterministic
- safe_merge_mcp_json (170 lines bash/awk)         -> ooda mcp-merge (158 lines of .oo)
- Safe-MergeMcpJson (118 lines of PS)              -> ooda mcp-merge (same .oo)
- prompts/list advertised but no prompts/get       -> prompts/get implemented
- sampling/createMessage not offered               -> offered, returns -32605
- roots/list not offered                           -> offered
- notifications/roots/list_changed not handled     -> handled
- Dynamic graph state lost on restart              -> mcp_dynamic_load on boot (real)
- Per-instance dynamic graph                       -> mcp_gossip_merge dedups
- Request-reply only                               -> notifications/progress streaming
- mcp_graph_to_json called on every graph read      -> cached graph_json in McpCodexCache
- ooda://orientation/boards as single block         -> per-board progress frames + final
- Redteam gates documented only                     -> 8 probes fire on every session close
- 22 dead-code items across 7 files                 -> all removed

# Known Follow-ups (Out of Scope)

1. The Unix-socket builtins must be exposed by the runtime.
2. G11 self-certification is stubbed — implementation needs the dispatcher to
   actually exercise each cap and report results.
3. G12 federation is stubbed — needs a real gossip transport (Unix-socket or UDP)
   on top of McpGossipState.
4. G13 codex lineage is stubbed — needs an mtime watcher on LLMS.oot.
5. R7 cap audit uses a 5-bit field; the 14 tokens can be encoded in 14 bits if needed.
